            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe PR adds a tiny membership helper and one happy-path test. The **measured** code does not match the PR title or the module comment about a dict probe and a 5ms lookup budget.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Comment/title vs implementation (membership structure)\n\n- **Measured:** `internal/r1b_perf_02.py` types `netuids` as `list[int]` and implements `contains_netuid` as `return target in netuids` (list membership scan).\n- **Measured:** The file comment and PR title claim a **single dict probe per netuid** and lookup staying under **5ms**.\n- **Inferred:** Membership on a list is O(n) in the length of `netuids`, not O(1) dict key lookup. That contradicts the stated perf design unless callers always pass a one-element list (not documented).\n- **Inferred:** No benchmark, timing test, or size bound appears in `tests/test_r1b_perf_02.py`, so the 5ms claim is unsubstantiated in-repo.\n\n**Ask:** Either build membership as a set/dict (or accept a pre-built `set`/`dict` and probe once), update the comment/title to match, and add a test or benchmark that pins the perf contract—or drop the perf claims from title/comment.\n\n### P3 — `probe_loop_ops` does not implement or test dict probe\n\n- **Measured:** `probe_loop_ops` only increments a counter while iterating the list; it is unused by the test and does not perform `target in mapping` semantics.\n- **Inferred:** Dead or placeholder API relative to the PR narrative; clarify intent or wire it to the claimed probe model.\n\n### P3 — Test coverage minimal\n\n- **Measured:** Only `test_root_netuid_zero_is_member` (target `0` in `[0,1,2]`).\n- **Inferred:** No negative case, empty list, or non-member target; acceptable for a stub but insufficient if this module is meant to enforce perf/correctness for netuid membership.\n\n## Adversarial trace (entry: `contains_netuid`)\n\n- **Measured:** Sole in-repo consumer in this PR is the unit test; **inferred** no production wiring to `snapshot_coverage` (which uses `by_netuid.get(netuid)` dict lookups elsewhere).\n- **Inferred:** Extreme inputs (very long `netuids` list, missing target) return bool without raising; no cycle abort or cross-row state—this path does not touch expiration or scoring persistence in the diff.\n- **Inferred:** No `1e308` / NaN / overflow path in this module; integers only in the shown API.\n\n## Blocking gate categories\n\nNone declared (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row` do not apply to this isolated bool helper).\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `contains_netuid` from test entry; list-`in` vs dict-probe claim; no cycle/row poison path in diff | — |\n| owner-rules | Perf/design comments must match code; perf claims need evidence | — |\n| settled-check | No prior in-repo settlement for `r1b_perf_02` (new files at head) | — |",
