      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on PR 9414 at head `e5fb689d959bd048fb3e2ca9d0fac0bb452df15c`.\n\n**Core issue (measured):** The PR title and comment in `internal/r1b_perf_02.py` promise a **single dict probe** and lookup under **5ms**, but `contains_netuid` uses `target in netuids` on a **`list[int]`**, which is a linear scan, not one dict lookup. There is no timing or benchmark test backing the 5ms claim.\n\n**Secondary (measured / inferred):** `probe_loop_ops` only counts list iterations and is unused by tests; coverage is a single “root netuid 0 is member” case. The new module is not wired into production paths such as `snapshot_coverage` (which already uses dict `.get` for netuids). No blocking gate categories (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) apply.\n\n**Recommendation:** Align implementation with the dict-probe story (set/dict or one probe on a mapping), align title/comment with reality, and add tests or a benchmark—or remove the perf claims.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after posting; the formal **MODIFY** verdict was accepted by `post_verdict`.",
