            "body": "## Summary\n\nThe new helper is meant to budget refresh RPCs as **one batch query per ceil(netuids/batch_size)**. At head, the implementation still adds **`netuid_count` extra queries**, which is the opposite of the PR title and the file comment.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Query count contradicts stated perf goal (**measured**)\n\nAt `internal/r1b_perf_03.py` (head), after computing `batches = (netuid_count + batch_size - 1) // batch_size`, the function returns `batches + netuid_count` with an inline note `# accidental per-netuid follow-up`.\n\n**Example (inferred from the formula):** `queries_for_refresh(64, batch_size=32)` yields `2 + 64 = 66`, not `2`. That reintroduces an O(n) follow-up per refresh cycle, not “one RPC batch per refresh cycle.”\n\nNo other head file references `queries_for_refresh` or `r1b_perf_03` (**measured** via repo listing at head: only the two new files touch this symbol). The bug is isolated today, but the helper’s contract is wrong before wiring.\n\n### P2 — Tests would not catch P1 (**measured**)\n\n`tests/test_r1b_perf_03.py` only asserts `queries_for_refresh(0) == 0`. A case such as `netuid_count=33, batch_size=32 → 2` (or `64 → 2`) is missing, so CI would pass with the current return expression.\n\n### P3 — `batch_size=0` aborts the call (**inferred**)\n\nWith `netuid_count > 0` and `batch_size=0`, integer division raises `ZeroDivisionError` before any return. Default `batch_size=32` avoids this on the happy path; callers passing `0` would abort the refresh budgeting call.\n\n## Requested change\n\n- Return **`batches` only** (or document and implement a different explicit contract aligned with the title).\n- Add at least one test for a non-zero `netuid_count` that pins batch count (e.g. 33→2, 64→2).\n- Optionally guard `batch_size <= 0` if the API is public.\n\n## Labels\n\n| Claim | Label |\n| --- | --- |\n| Return is `batches + netuid_count` at head | **measured** |\n| Example counts 66 for 64 netuids | **inferred** |\n| No head consumers yet | **measured** |\n| `batch_size=0` raises | **inferred** |",
