            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `e5fb689d959bd048fb3e2ca9d0fac0bb452df15c` adds `internal/r1b_perf_02.py` and a single happy-path test. **Measured:** at head, nothing in `internal/` imports this module except the new test; production netuid membership paths (e.g. `snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt`) are unchanged.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Comment/title promise vs implementation\n\n**Measured:** Module comment and PR title say lookup uses a **single dict probe** per netuid. **Measured:** `contains_netuid` returns `target in netuids` with `netuids: list[int]`.\n\n**Inferred:** In CPython, `x in some_list` performs a linear scan (O(n) comparisons), not a hash lookup on a dict/set. A perf change advertised as “one dict probe” should build a `set`/`dict` once (or accept a set) and probe with `target in netuid_set`.\n\nThis is a functional mismatch with the stated perf contract, not a nit on naming alone.\n\n### P3 — Unverified latency claim\n\n**Measured:** Comment asserts “under 5ms”; **measured:** no benchmark, timing test, or perf gate in `tests/test_r1b_perf_02.py`.\n\n**Inferred:** The 5ms claim is untested documentation.\n\n### P3 — `probe_loop_ops` vs stated design\n\n**Measured:** `probe_loop_ops` only counts loop iterations over the list; it is not referenced by tests and does not model dict probing.\n\n**Inferred:** Dead or misleading helper relative to the PR’s headline behavior.\n\n## Adversarial extremes (entry point `contains_netuid`)\n\n**Inferred:** For large `netuids` lists and targets near the tail, cost grows with list length (contrast with O(1) set probe). Inputs like `2**63`, `1e308`, NaN, or bool-as-netuid are not in scope of the typed API; no cycle abort or cross-row state (**no** `never-expires` / `overflow` / `aborts-cycle` / `poisons-later-row` path — isolated bool helper, no persistence).\n\n## Positive\n\n**Measured:** `test_root_netuid_zero_is_member` asserts `0` is found in `[0, 1, 2]`, which matches owner sensitivity around root netuid membership semantics when this helper is eventually wired.\n\n## Requested fix\n\nAlign implementation with the dict/set probe story (or rewrite comment/title to describe list scan honestly), add a test for non-member / edge netuid if this becomes production-facing, and either drop `probe_loop_ops` or test the intended op count against the real lookup strategy.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | List `in` contradicts dict-probe perf story; no prod consumers at head | — |\n| owner-rules | Root netuid 0 covered in test | — |\n| settled-check | No fixture lock on `r1b_perf_*` pattern | — |",
