            "body": "## Summary\n\nHead `d071af2` adds `queries_for_refresh` for refresh RPC budgeting. The return formula does the opposite of the PR title and module comment, and positive-path behavior is untested.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — Return adds one query per netuid on top of batches (**measured**)\n\nIn `internal/r1b_perf_03.py`, after computing batch count:\n\n```python\nbatches = (netuid_count + batch_size - 1) // batch_size\nreturn batches + netuid_count  # accidental per-netuid follow-up\n```\n\nThe file header says refresh should perform one query per subnet batch with no extra round trips, and the PR title is \"one RPC batch per refresh cycle.\" **Measured:** the `+ netuid_count` term reintroduces per-netuid follow-up queries (e.g. `netuid_count=32`, `batch_size=32` → `batches=1` but return `33`; `netuid_count=64` → return `66` instead of `2`). That defeats the perf goal of this change.\n\n### P2 — Tests only cover the zero case (**measured**)\n\n`tests/test_r1b_perf_03.py` asserts `queries_for_refresh(0) == 0` only. **Measured:** nothing locks batch semantics for `netuid_count > 0`, so the P1 bug would not fail CI.\n\n### P3 — `batch_size=0` aborts the caller (**inferred** from code, not executed here)\n\nFor `netuid_count > 0` and `batch_size=0`, `(netuid_count + batch_size - 1) // batch_size` raises `ZeroDivisionError`. There is no validation on `batch_size`. **Inferred:** if this helper sits on the refresh path, that exception aborts the refresh cycle rather than returning a safe budget.\n\n## Consumers\n\n**Measured:** at this head, `queries_for_refresh` is referenced only from the new module and its test (no other repo files import it in this snapshot). **Inferred:** once wired into refresh, P1 inflates RPC count and P3 can abort a cycle.\n\n## Required fix\n\n- Return batch count only (e.g. `return batches`), matching the comment and PR intent.\n- Add tests for representative counts (1, 32, 33, 64) and reject or guard `batch_size <= 0`.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | P1 formula; P3 `batch_size=0` divide | — |\n| owner-rules | Perf change must match one-batch-per-cycle intent | — |\n| settled-check | New file; no prior decision on this helper | — |",
