      "finalText": "Review complete for [PR 9415](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9415) at head `d071af2dd0295d253b8bad0ce348e4fd458db39a`.\n\n**Verdict: FAIL** (posted via `post_verdict`).\n\n**Main issue (measured):** `queries_for_refresh` computes batch count correctly, then returns `batches + netuid_count` with a comment calling out “accidental per-netuid follow-up.” That adds one extra query per netuid and contradicts the PR title and the module note about one query per batch (e.g. 32 netuids → 33 queries instead of 1).\n\n**Other issues:** Tests only cover `netuid_count == 0`, so the bug would not fail CI. **Inferred:** `batch_size=0` with positive `netuid_count` raises `ZeroDivisionError` with no guard — declared under `aborts-cycle`.\n\n**Fix direction:** Return `batches` only, add tests for typical batch boundaries, and validate `batch_size > 0`.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after posting; MC’s formal FAIL is on the PR for this head. Author should fix and push a new head for another gate pass.",
