            "body": "MODIFY\n\n## Summary\nHead `8badbf736caf4de93b619136c12880d2ee4d1af2` adds `internal/r1b_perf_04.py` and a single test. I tried to prove the change safe for validity-row merge; the complexity claim and key coercion do not hold up against the repo’s existing `validity_map` handling.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P2 — Unguarded `int(k)` on map keys (`aborts-cycle`)\n**Measured:** `merged_netuids` does `out.append(int(k))` for every key in `validity_map` with no `str(k).isdigit()` (or equivalent) guard.\n**Measured:** Production membership loading already filters with `str(key).isdigit()` before `int(key)` on `snap.validity_map` entries (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`).\n**Inferred:** Any non-numeric or empty string key raises `ValueError` and aborts the caller; if this helper is wired into a scoring or refresh cycle (the PR title’s intent), one bad row aborts the whole cycle instead of skipping the key.\n\n### P2 — “O(1) constant-time merge” does not match the implementation\n**Measured:** `merged_netuids` iterates all keys (O(n)) and `out.sort()` (O(n log n)). `merge_loop_ops` counts keys (O(n)).\n**Inferred:** The module comment and PR title misstate complexity; this is not constant-time merge.\n\n### P3 — Not connected to a production merge entry point\n**Measured:** At head, only `tests/test_r1b_perf_04.py` imports `merged_netuids`; nothing under `internal/council/` or elsewhere calls this module.\n**Inferred:** The perf win is unproven until the helper replaces an actual hot-path merge and is covered by behavior tests (non-digit keys, empty map, root `0`).\n\n### P3 — Test coverage is minimal\n**Measured:** One assertion that `0` appears in the merged list for digit-string keys only.\n**Inferred:** No test for sort order, `merge_loop_ops`, or failure modes.\n\n## What would unblock PASS\n- Align key parsing with the established `isdigit()` guard (or document and enforce a typed netuid key contract).\n- Fix or remove the O(1) claim; if the goal is O(n) key collection without redundant work, say that explicitly.\n- Wire into the real validity merge call site (or scope the PR as test-only stub) and extend tests accordingly.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Unguarded `int(k)` aborts on bad keys; sort makes merge O(n log n), not O(1); no prod consumer at head | — |\n| owner-rules | Validity map keys must be handled like membership receipt (digit guard before int) | — |\n| settled-check | No settled doc in fixture repo for R1B perf-04; compared to existing `validity_map` pattern in tree | — |",
