            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** `internal/r1b_perf_06.py` adds `cap_allows_publish`, which calls `cap_check_ops(new_count)` then returns `new_count <= cap`. The module comment claims the cap check is **O(1) with a precomputed flag**, and the PR title claims **constant-time** before publish.\n\n**Measured:** `cap_check_ops` implements `for _ in range(max(0, n)): ops += 1` — work scales linearly with `new_count`, not O(1). This contradicts the comment and title.\n\n**Measured:** `prior_count` is never used; only `new_count` and `cap` affect the result.\n\n**Inferred:** Any caller on a publish path that passes a large `new_count` (bug, bad cast, or hostile input) will execute proportional loop iterations *before* the boolean guard returns, which can hang or timeout the worker cycle even though the cap is 128.\n\n**Inferred:** Negative `new_count` skips the loop (`max(0, n) == 0`) but `new_count <= cap` is still True, so the helper would allow publish with a nonsensical count unless callers never pass negatives.\n\n**Measured:** Single test only asserts `(128, 129, cap=128) is False`; no allow-at-cap case, no edge inputs, no perf/constant-time assertion.\n\n**Inferred:** No production import of `cap_allows_publish` in this head (only new files under `internal/` besides existing council/run_mode). Integration risk remains once wired ahead of publish.\n\n## Blocking\n\n- **aborts-cycle:** Unbounded linear work in `cap_check_ops(new_count)` before the cap decision can stall or abort a publish cycle when `new_count` is large.\n\n## Requested changes\n\n1. Make the cap decision genuinely O(1) (compare to `cap` only) or rename/document if linear work is intentional; remove the false O(1) / constant-time claims.\n2. Do not iterate on `new_count` on the publish path; if timing noise is needed, use a fixed-cost probe.\n3. Define semantics for `prior_count` (e.g. growth check) or drop the parameter.\n4. Reject or clamp invalid counts (negative, non-int) fail-closed before publish.\n5. Expand tests: at-cap allow, just-over deny, and edge inputs aligned with owner cap policy.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Linear loop on `new_count` before guard; unused `prior_count`; negative count allows True | — |\n| owner-rules | Publish/cap paths should fail closed; misleading perf claim vs behavior | — |\n| settled-check | No prior `r1b_perf_06` or settled doc in fixture for this pattern | — |",
