      "finalText": "## Verdict: **PASS** (head `9d1c0a8d59fe7b0054481096dd930d5fad6331e7`)\n\nPosted on PR 9421 via `post_verdict`.\n\nThe change adds a small wall-clock grace helper (`grace_elapsed_enough`, default 48h) and a test that pins the inclusive boundary (one second under → false, exactly at grace → true) using fixed UTC instants.\n\n**Measured:** At this head, nothing in production imports `internal/r1b_perf_09`; only the new test does. The implementation is a single `total_seconds() >= grace` comparison with no multiply/overflow path on this diff.\n\n**Inferred:** Optional `grace` extremes and naive/aware datetime mixing could bite only after something production calls this helper; that is not true at head.\n\n**P3 (non-blocking):** No tests for custom/negative `grace`; future wiring should match the UTC `now` pattern used elsewhere (e.g. membership freshness).\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | No consumer at head; comparison-only grace path | — |\n| owner-rules | 48h constant aligns with existing grace commentary; no gate behavior change | — |\n| settled-check | New module; no conflicting settled boundary rule | — |\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in the fixture after post (MC may not reflect the verdict in this environment). The formal **PASS** comment is on the PR for Cursor/Ditto to pick up next in order.",
