            "verdict": "MODIFY",
            "body": "## Summary\n\n**measured:** PR adds `internal/r1b_perf_02.py` and `tests/test_r1b_perf_02.py` only. Nothing at head imports `contains_netuid`, `probe_loop_ops`, or `r1b_perf_02` (repo listing at head is four files under `internal/` plus this test).\n\n**measured:** `contains_netuid` is implemented as `return target in netuids` with `netuids: list[int]`.\n\n**inferred:** Membership on a Python `list` is a linear scan (O(n) comparisons), not a single O(1) hash lookup on a `dict`/`set` as the module comment, PR title, and perf narrative claim.\n\n**measured:** `probe_loop_ops` counts one op per list element in a loop; it is not used in tests and does not implement or measure a dict probe.\n\n**measured:** The only test asserts `contains_netuid([0, 1, 2], 0) is True`. There is no negative member case, no assertion on probe count, and no timing bound backing “under 5ms”.\n\n## Adversarial entry point (`contains_netuid`)\n\nTraced the only called symbol from tests through its body (no other callers at head).\n\n| Input sketch | Abort cycle? | Poison later row? |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Empty list, any `target` | **inferred:** returns False; no exception | **inferred:** no persisted state |\n| Huge list, `target` at end | **inferred:** slow, not abort | none |\n| `target` not in list | False | none |\n| Non-int `target` at runtime (hint ignored) | **inferred:** `in` still defined; no multiply/overflow in this function | none |\n\nNo path here touches cycle globals, receipt TTL, or scoring state from `snapshot_coverage.py`. Numeric overflow (`inf`/`NaN` from arithmetic) does not arise in this two-line membership check.\n\n## Owner alignment\n\n**inferred:** Perf/honesty framing elsewhere in the repo treats lookup claims as binding on the actual structure used (`snapshot_coverage` uses `set`/`dict` for membership-style work). Shipping a comment and title that say “dict probe” while probing a list is a documentation/contract defect for a perf-titled change.\n\n## Required fixes before PASS\n\n1. If the contract is O(1) per netuid: build a `set` or dict view once and probe that (and test probe count or behavior), **or** retitle/recomment to “list scan” and drop the 5ms/dict-probe claim.\n2. Either wire `contains_netuid` into the real lookup path you intend to optimize, or document why this module stands alone.\n3. Add tests for absent `target`, and align or remove `probe_loop_ops` so it does not contradict the stated model.\n\nNo blocking gate tags (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`) — failure mode is wrong perf story and incomplete tests, not scoring poison.",
