            "body": "MODIFY — perf claim and merge helper do not match code or existing validity-map handling.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **False O(1) claim (measured, P1).** `merged_netuids` iterates every key, coerces with `int(k)`, then `out.sort()`. That is **O(n log n)** in the number of keys, not constant time. `merge_loop_ops` is **O(n)**. The module comment and PR title assert O(1) constant-time merge; that is incorrect on its face.\n\n2. **No validity-row merge (measured, P2).** The change only collects dict keys into a sorted int list. It does not read or merge validity **rows** (e.g. `validity`, grace, expiry fields). Nothing under `internal/` imports `r1b_perf_04` at this head except the new test — so this is not wired to the snapshot / universe cycle entry points that already consume `snap.validity_map` in `internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`.\n\n3. **Unguarded `int(k)` (inferred, P1 — blocking).** Real entry point for this module is `merged_netuids(validity_map)`. Any non-numeric key (`\"\"`, `\"NaN\"`, `\"1.5\"`, arbitrary strings) raises **ValueError** and aborts the caller. Existing membership code gates keys with `str(key).isdigit()` before `int(key)` when walking `validity_map`. This helper skips that seam.\n\n4. **Root netuid semantics (inferred, P2).** The test requires `0 in merged_netuids(...)`. Scoring membership paths in `snapshot_coverage` deliberately exclude root via `int(n) > 0`. If this helper is adopted as the scoring netuid list without an explicit filter, root would enter downstream sets contrary to pinned rules.\n\n5. **Coverage (measured, P3).** One happy-path test; no cases for bad keys, empty map, or complexity/ops expectations for `merge_loop_ops`.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `merged_netuids` / `merge_loop_ops`; no prod importers; non-digit keys abort via `int(k)` | — |\n| owner-rules | Validity-map key handling should follow `isdigit()` gating; scoring set excludes root (`> 0`) | — |\n| settled-check | Fixture repo — no locks/roadmap files to consult | skipped: no settled docs in fixture |\n\n## Ask\n\nDrop or correct the O(1) claim; align merge semantics with actual validity-row fields; guard keys like `load_membership_receipt`; clarify root policy vs scoring; add tests for invalid keys and intended complexity.",
