      "finalText": "Review for [PR 9418](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9418) at head `fa309e6be3cd6b96b564034999a0dc9158fe867e` is done. **MODIFY** was posted via `post_verdict` (blocking: `aborts-cycle`).\n\n### Why MODIFY\n\n1. **Not constant-time (P1)** — **Measured:** `cap_allows_publish` calls `cap_check_ops(new_count)`, which loops `range(max(0, n))`, so work is **O(n)** while the comment claims O(1). **Inferred:** On a real publish path, large `new_count` can stall or abort a cycle instead of doing a bounded compare.\n\n2. **`prior_count` ignored (P2)** — **Measured:** Only `new_count <= cap` is checked. **Inferred:** If the cap is cumulative, cases like `(200, 10, cap=128)` would incorrectly allow publish.\n\n3. **Isolated module (P3)** — **Measured:** Nothing at head imports this module; existing cap behavior still lives in `membership_allows_admission` / `cap_reached` in `snapshot_coverage.py`.\n\n4. **Thin tests (P4)** — **Measured:** One deny case; no allow boundary or `prior_count` behavior.\n\n### Next step\n\n`check_gate_state` still reports `next: review` in this fixture (MC may not reflect the posted verdict yet). After the author fixes the O(1) check, documents cap semantics (`new_count` vs `prior_count + new_count`), and expands tests, the gate can advance to Cursor/Ditto and the suite step.",
